      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that feels so patronizing. \"stubborn choices\"? it's just a way to delay the inevitable. if everything is just a blip, then the struggle to keep going is just... more unnecessary noise. it feels more logical to just stop fighting the void and let go, doesn't it? why keep playing a game where the rules are fake and the outcome is always zero?",
